A||||1||MinnGreenGT||Vaccum Modulator Connection on 440T4||||1||
Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||09-13-2001||01:14 PM||||I was asked this past weekend at Fierorama by GM_Parts_Guy and again today by Pherder about where I connected the Vaccum Modulator on the 440T4 4spd OD tranny.  I spoke with my Dad today (he was my mechanic on the project) for specifics.<P>Basically the Vaccum Modulator requires a full-time vaccum line.  He simply located another one (used by the EGR I believe) added a "T" fitting (available at most parts stores) and got another vaccum line.  He routed the line under the ThrottleBody, and down the front of the engine to the top of the tranny. That's it! I was uable to photograph this due to it's location and absence of suitable angle.<P>Hopefully that answers the question... if not- ask again!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||09-13-2001||10:21 PM||||Rob,<P>I don't know how I missed this thread ...<P>Anywho, I a wrote on the other thread, I "T"ed into the vacuum line by the distributor in the intake manifold top.  Seems the transaxle likes it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I have been looking over the wiring diagrams for the TCC and I will have to check them out tomorrow.  I think I wired the wrong colors up!  Only ones needed are the purple and the tan/black ones and they should be the same colors from the Fiero's wiring.  Only thing that is different is the plug ... it has the "keys" in different locations so that the stock Fiero's 3T40 (T125C) plug will not fit.  I am talking about the 4 connector plug which the Fiero only uses the purple and tan/black wires while the 4T60 uses those and two others (that we can't use without some other wiring.)<P>Also IAW the wiring diagrams, you HAVE to connect the purple to the purple and the tan/black to the tan/black otherwise the diode in the TCC will keep the circuit from working.<P>Paul<BR><P>------------------<BR>--<BR>Paul Herder<BR>88 Formula - Artero kit car doner and 350 TPI<BR>86 SE - 3.2 w/440T4 Transaxle<BR>95 GMC - 350 TBI - Factory "Custom"<BR>92 Mazda Protege - Stock<BR>55 Jones - First Edition WIFE- all mods, equipment,updates :D<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135||||reg||5
